From: ihexon <zzheasy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: hdmi-codec: handle empty ELD during PCM startup

DW HDMI supplies an all-zero ELD when no sink is connected. PCM startup
nevertheless parses it as a monitor description and reports an unknown
ELD version on every playback probe. The existing PCM constraints and
channel map already support a stereo fallback for an empty ELD.

Treat the entirely empty buffer as absent monitor information, clearing
the parsed state rather than parsing version zero. Keep the fallback so
audio services can discover the output before a monitor is plugged in.
Nonempty ELDs still go through the parser, including malformed ones, and
the hotplug callback continues to refresh the monitor capabilities.

Signed-off-by: ihexon <zzheasy@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/hdmi-codec.c b/sound/soc/codecs/hdmi-codec.c
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/hdmi-codec.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/hdmi-codec.c
@@ -471,8 +471,12 @@ static int hdmi_codec_startup(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream,
 		if (ret)
 			goto err;
 
-		snd_parse_eld(dai->dev, &hcp->eld_parsed,
-			      hcp->eld, sizeof(hcp->eld));
+		/* An unplugged bridge may return an entirely empty ELD. */
+		if (memchr_inv(hcp->eld, 0, sizeof(hcp->eld)))
+			snd_parse_eld(dai->dev, &hcp->eld_parsed,
+				      hcp->eld, sizeof(hcp->eld));
+		else
+			memset(&hcp->eld_parsed, 0, sizeof(hcp->eld_parsed));
 
 		ret = snd_pcm_hw_constraint_eld(substream->runtime, hcp->eld);
 		if (ret)
